msgstr "国家数据集"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid "National Health Workforce Accounts (NHWA) dataset. Not a second registry: an analytical linking and indexing dataset that builds on CDE-HWR. The HWR identifier is the key that links records about the same worker held in other data systems, which the NHWA handbook lists as potential data sources: the health workforce registry or database, facility administrative records and HMIS, professional council registers, labour force surveys and population census. From these, the 29 NHWA indicators in 4 modules are computed (1 stock and flow; 2 education; 3 finance and expenditures; 4 working conditions, governance and leadership) and reported nationally and to the WHO NHWA platform. Source: WHO, National health workforce accounts: a handbook, 2nd ed., 2023 (ISBN 9789240081291): the NHWA is \"a system by which countries progressively improve the availability, quality, and use of data on health workforce through monitoring of a set of indicators\", using diverse existing data sources (core principles: multi-sectoral governance, progressive implementation, no primary data collection)."
msgstr "国家卫生人力账户（NHWA）数据集。不是第二个登记系统，而是基于 CDE-HWR 的分析性关联与索引数据集。HWR 标识符是关联其他数据系统中关于同一工作者的记录的键，NHWA 手册将这些系统列为潜在数据来源：卫生人力登记系统或数据库、机构行政记录和 HMIS、专业委员会注册名册、劳动力调查和人口普查。据此计算 4 个模块中的 29 项 NHWA 指标（1 存量与流量；2 教育；3 财务与支出；4 工作条件、治理与领导），并在国内及向 WHO NHWA 平台报告。来源：WHO，《国家卫生人力账户：手册》，第 2 版，2023 年（ISBN 9789240081291）：NHWA 是“一个国家通过监测一组指标，逐步提高卫生人力数据的可用性、质量和使用的体系”，使用多种现有数据来源（核心原则：多部门治理、渐进实施、不开展原始数据收集）。"

