#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid "The ability to record the act of preparing and giving stock to a patient or consumer. This includes the list of minimums that any system providing direct distribution of medical goods should be able to provide for."
msgstr "记录准备库存并将其交给患者或消费者这一行为的能力。其中包括任何直接分发医疗物资的系统应能提供的最低功能清单。"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid "The ability to track a product’s journey from origin to end-user – is crucial for non-profit and Public Health work. Whether distributing medicines, food aid, or other essential goods, organizations need end-to-end visibility to ensure products are authentic, safely handled, and actually reach intended beneficiaries. By assigning unique identifiers to products and capturing their movements in a digital system, stakeholders can quickly pinpoint where an item is at any given time or isolate issues (like a bad batch of medication) and initiate targeted recalls[1]. In low-resource settings, improving traceability boosts trust and reduces fraud, theft, and counterfeiting – common problems that undermine humanitarian efforts[2][3]. Overall, robust traceability systems enhance transparency and accountability, which are core values in Public Health supply chains."
msgstr "追踪产品从原产地到最终用户全过程的能力，对非营利和公共卫生工作至关重要。无论是分发药品、粮食援助还是其他基本物资，组织都需要端到端的可见性，以确保产品真实、得到安全处理并切实送达目标受益人。通过为产品分配唯一标识符并在数字系统中采集其流转信息，利益相关方可以快速确定某件物品在任一时刻的位置，或隔离问题（如一批不合格药品）并启动有针对性的召回[1]。在资源匮乏的环境中，提高可追溯性可以增强信任，减少欺诈、盗窃和假冒——这些是破坏人道主义工作的常见问题[2][3]。总体而言，健全的可追溯性系统能够增强透明度和问责，而这正是公共卫生供应链的核心价值。"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid "The ability to track key performance indicators, produce standard reports and allow for custom report development and analytics on the data. All threshold KPIs should be configurable by the administrator of the system."
msgstr "跟踪关键绩效指标、生成标准报告，并支持基于数据开发自定义报告和分析的能力。所有阈值类 KPI 均应可由系统管理员配置。"

#: archimate/scripts/templates/archimate.js:0
msgid "The Archi model file"
msgstr "Archi 模型文件"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid ""
"The benefit or utility gained by a stakeholder from using a service, product, or capability.\n"
"\n"
"Value captures why a goal or capability matters and who benefits. Value can be monetary, but in health contexts it often reflects non-monetary benefits such as trust, usability, or equity. \n"
"\n"
"For example, a citizen values secure access to their data, while a health worker values having a complete clinical history at the point of care.\n"
msgstr ""
"利益相关方通过使用服务、产品或能力而获得的收益或效用。\n"
"\n"
"价值说明某个目标或能力为何重要以及谁从中受益。价值可以是货币性的，但在卫生领域往往体现为非货币性收益，例如信任、易用性或公平。\n"
"\n"
"例如，公民重视安全地访问自己的数据，而卫生工作者重视在医疗服务点获得完整的临床病史。\n"
"\n"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid "The capabilities necessary to managing the flow of stock into the facility, its current disposition, and the flow of stock out of the facility."
msgstr "管理库存流入机构、当前处置状况以及库存流出机构所需的能力。"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid "The capabilities necessary to managing the flow of stock into the health facility, its current disposition, and the flow of stock out of the facility. In this case, outbound processing describes when a facility is also acting as a local redistribution hub that is able to share or move stock to other facilities."
msgstr "管理库存流入卫生机构、当前处置状况以及库存流出机构所需的能力。在这种情况下，出库处理是指机构同时作为本地再分配中心，能够向其他机构共享或调拨库存。"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid "The capabilities of the RA's Integrated View that the journeys realize."
msgstr "旅程所实现的 RA 集成视图中的能力。"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid "The clinician abroad who gives the birth doses and hands over the signed paper DVC (J1)."
msgstr "国外的临床医生：接种出生剂次并交付已签名的纸质 DVC（J1）。"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid "The clinician abroad who scans the family's QR and reads the child's records (J4.1)."
msgstr "国外的临床医生：扫描家庭的 QR 码并读取儿童的记录（J4.1）。"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid ""
"The concrete offering, which is made available to stakeholders. \n"
"\n"
"It bundles together services, data, and rules into a package that delivers value. Products make capabilities consumable by users. \n"
"\n"
"For example, the Trusted Personal Health Record or the National Surveillance Dashboard are products delivered in the DPI-H context.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"A product represents a coherent collection of services and/or passive structure elements, accompanied by a contract, which is offered as a whole to (internal or external) customers. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This definition covers both intangible, services-based, or information products that are common in information-intensive organizations, as well as tangible, physical products. A financial or information product consists of a collection of services along with a contract that specifies the characteristics, rights, and requirements associated with the product. “Buying” a product gives the customer the right to use the associated services. Generally, the product element is used to specify a product type. The number of product types in an organization is typically relatively stable compared to the processes that realize or support the products. “Buying” is usually one of the services associated with a product which results in a new instance of that product (belonging to a specific customer). Similarly, there may be services to modify or destroy a product. A product may aggregate or compose business services, application services, technology services, business objects, data objects, and technology passive structure elements (artifacts and material), as well as a contract. Hence a product may aggregate or compose elements from other layers than the Business Layer. A value may be associated with a product. The name of a product is usually the name used in the communication with customers, or possibly a more generic noun (e.g., “travel insurance”).\n"
msgstr ""
"提供给利益相关方的具体产品。\n"
"\n"
"它将服务、数据和规则捆绑成一个交付价值的组合包。产品使能力可供用户使用。\n"
"\n"
"例如，可信个人健康记录或国家监测仪表板就是 DPI-H 背景下交付的产品。\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"产品代表一组连贯的服务和/或被动结构元素，并附带一份合同，作为整体提供给（内部或外部）客户。\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"这一定义既涵盖信息密集型组织中常见的无形产品、基于服务的产品或信息产品，也涵盖有形的实物产品。金融产品或信息产品由一组服务以及一份规定与该产品相关的特征、权利和要求的合同组成。“购买”一个产品赋予客户使用相关服务的权利。通常，产品元素用于规定一种产品类型。与实现或支持产品的流程相比，组织中的产品类型数量通常相对稳定。“购买”通常是与产品相关的服务之一，其结果是产生该产品的一个新实例（属于特定客户）。同样，也可能存在修改或销毁产品的服务。产品可以聚合或组合业务服务、应用服务、技术服务、业务对象、数据对象和技术被动结构元素（制品和材料），以及一份合同。因此，产品可以聚合或组合业务层以外其他层的元素。价值可以与产品相关联。产品的名称通常是与客户沟通时使用的名称，也可以是更通用的名词（例如“旅行保险”）。\n"
"\n"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid "The demonstrator’s journeys as business processes: the people assigned to each (its BPMN lanes), the DPI-H RA stakeholders those people belong to, and the RA capabilities it realizes. The systems that serve each journey are in that journey’s own view."
msgstr "以业务流程表示的演示项目旅程：分配给每个旅程的人员（其 BPMN 泳道），这些人员所属的 DPI-H RA 利益相关方，以及它所实现的 RA 能力。为每个旅程服务的系统见该旅程自己的视图。"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid "The demonstrator's user journeys, one BPMN process each, in processes/content/."
msgstr "演示项目的用户旅程，每个旅程一个 BPMN 流程，位于 processes/content/。"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid ""
"The deployed IT system that provides the functionality. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Components encapsulate logic and data, and expose their behavior through services. They are modular, replaceable, and reusable. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"For example, the Client Registry, Interoperability Middleware, or Terminology Serviceer are application components within DPI-H.\n"
msgstr ""
"提供功能的已部署 IT 系统。\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"组件封装逻辑和数据，并通过服务公开其行为。组件是模块化、可替换和可复用的。\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"例如，服务对象登记系统、互操作性中间件或术语服务都是 DPI-H 中的应用组件。\n"
"\n"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid "The DHSC architecture framework of the supply chain DTH (Fig. 14, PDF 34), based on TOGAF and OpenHIE. Groupings and members as drawn; no relationships beyond membership are asserted."
msgstr "供应链 DTH 的 DHSC 架构框架（图 14，PDF 34），基于 TOGAF 和 OpenHIE。分组和成员按原图绘制；除成员关系外未声明其他关系。"

#: archimate/0.1.0/model.json:0
msgid "The DPI-H RA’s own building blocks, by the layers of its Integrated View (Fig. 3.2): generic, no country’s. Each country’s instance of a block specializes it."
msgstr "DPI-H RA 自身的构建块，按其集成视图（图 3.2）的各层排列：通用，不属于任何国家。各国的构建块实例是对它的特化。"

